+          "creation": "Parent reserved ownership manifest contains attempt/temp inode before helper Popen; helper immediately creates/updates lease-<attempt_id>.json with helper_pid,helper_lstart,pgid=helper_pid,port,start_ts. Install SIGTERM handler/EOF watcher first; if parent already died EOF is latched, do not launch serve. serve_proc=Popen(...,stdin=DEVNULL,start_new_session=False,env=serve_env) in same child_pgid; atomic fsync+replace adds serve_pid and serve_lstart BEFORE stdout handshake {\"serve_pid\":...,\"pgid\":...}, then parent lsof/READY/Auth. Check EOF before serve Popen, immediately after it, before/after lease publication/handshake and in <=0.25s monitor loop. No gap depends on parent surviving to publish child identity; helper owns serve Popen->lease publication. helper_proc denotes parent Popen object only; serve_proc denotes helper Popen object only. Helper argv=[sys.executable, \"-I\", str(Path(__file__).resolve()), \"--serve-helper\", attempt_id, str(port), ...]; start_new_session=True, child_pgid=helper_proc.pid. CLI dispatcher is inside if __name__ == \"__main__\": after existing import zen_catalog as zc and before main()/HTTP startup; all typed _run_serve_helper_cli(...) code resides directly in server.py, checked by Ruff/basedpyright with zero new Any/E402. No inline -c source, no new helper module. --serve-helper <attempt_id> follows script path at the front of ps argv, before port/other parameters; reaper verifies exact script realpath, argv position, full untruncated ps -ww command, attempt_id, UID/PID/lstart/PGID and manifest. Never put password or prompt in argv.",
